  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe gaming/computing sense (sense 1) is extremely common in everyday Japanese. セーブする means \"to save\" data or game progress. The opposite is ロードする (to load).\n\nThe sports sense (sense 2) is used mainly in baseball and soccer. In baseball, it refers to the official statistic for a relief pitcher who preserves a lead.\n\nNote that セーブ is NOT used for \"saving money\" (that is {節約|せつやく}する or {貯金|ちょきん}する) or \"saving someone\" (that is {助|たす}ける or {救|すく}う).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- セーブする: to save (data/game)\n- セーブデータ: save data, save file\n- セーブポイント: save point\n- オートセーブ: auto-save",
